{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3913","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3913","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3913\",\"parent_revision\":\"2458e5f1f83f6f834d903ac30ceda5e79d6318bfbf3b87850f57be68747cfd94\",\"root_revision\":\"2458e5f1f83f6f834d903ac30ceda5e79d6318bfbf3b87850f57be68747cfd94\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-25\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA targeted reconcile propagates a provider-side title change into the writer cache but does not propagate the provider-side body change.\\n\\nReproduction (observed in CI, not yet reproduced offline):\\n1. CI workflow `code-quality.yml`, job `e2e`, run id 36111244911. Preflight passed \u2014 token, sandbox identity and `.dh-e2e-sandbox` marker all validated.\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py::test_live_crud_persists_changes_and_preserves_other_sections`, phase \\\"pull observes an independent provider edit\\\".\\n3. The phase edits a real GitHub issue natively with PyGithub `issue.edit(title=..., body=...)`, setting both a new title and a new body.\\n4. It calls the MCP tool `backlog_pull` with `{\\\"selector\\\": \\\"#<companion>\\\"}`.\\n5. It calls `backlog_view` with the new title as a non-numeric selector, so the read is served from the cache the pull populated rather than refetching from the provider.\\n\\nObserved: the title lookup resolves and the returned title equals the new remote title, so the pull did see the provider edit and did write the new title. The returned body does not carry the provider's new body text. The assertion that fails is:\\n\\n    assert \\\"Provider edit not present in the writer cache.\\\" in str(pulled[\\\"body\\\"]), pulled\\n\\nThe returned dict carried a `description` field beginning with the run marker `<!-- dh-e2e-run:36111244911-1 -->`.\\n\\nImpact: a targeted pull reports success while leaving the cached body stale. Any consumer that reads an item after a pull, instead of refetching, sees pre-edit content. The whole lifecycle before this phase succeeded \u2014 labels created, issues created, plan comment posted, status set to in-progress, two grooms committed, `backlog_sync` published a queued mutation \u2014 so provider write access and the transport are not implicated.\\n\\nEvidence retained: `/tmp/e2eart/` from that run holds `preflight.log`, `pytest.log`, `junit.xml`, `cleanup.log`, and the per-test phase/response `.jsonl` journal.\\n\\nOpen question for grooming: whether production is wrong or the assertion is. `plugins/development-harness/docs/live-e2e-validation.md` states that raw issue bodies are human-owned and that grooming must not be tested as a body rewrite. If a deliberate \\\"remote body does not overwrite local content\\\" rule exists in the reconcile path, the correct outcome is a corrected assertion, not a production change.\\n\\nSecond, smaller defect in the same area: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` line 3 cites the runbook as `docs/live-e2e-validation.md`; the file is at `plugins/development-harness/docs/live-e2e-validation.md`.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Live e2e run 36111244911 against the private sandbox Jamie-BitFlight/test_project_experiment\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"688a7c6f0f89c50971438b64562f4f647215c19a3c2b91b1af2f15bdfd2198b8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCDkVg\"}"}